// Steps to Execute in Exams:

Have already:
Created AWS account
Configured S3, Rekognition, RDS, SNS
Tested AWS connection
Successfully executed on your Ubuntu system
Uploaded clean project to GitHub
Now:
Clone → Setup Python → Add AWS config → Update RDS IP → Run

Follow:
Step 1: Open Terminal and install basics
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y git python3 python3-pip python3-venv python3-dev build-essential cmake ffmpeg libgl1 libglib2.0-0 mysql-client netcat-openbsd

Step 2: Clone your GitHub project
cd ~/Documents
git clone https://github.com/MusaibParvez07/Cloud-Smart-Attendance-System.git
ls

Step 3: Create fresh virtual environment
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate

Step 4: Install dependencies
python -m pip install --upgrade pip setuptools wheel
pip install -r requirements.txt

Step 5: Create AWS config file
cp aws_config.example.json aws_config.json
nano aws_config.json
open and paste:
{
  "aws_access_key_id": "PASTE_YOUR_IAM_ACCESS_KEY_HERE",
  "aws_secret_access_key": "PASTE_YOUR_IAM_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY_HERE",
  "aws_region": "ap-south-1",

  "s3_bucket_name": "musaib-smart-attendance-faces-2026",
  "s3_region": "ap-south-1",

  "rds_host": "attendance-db.c184eaoq25qk.ap-south-1.rds.amazonaws.com",
  "rds_user": "admin",
  "rds_password": "PASTE_YOUR_RDS_PASSWORD_HERE",
  "rds_db_name": "attendance_db",

  "sns_topic_arn": "PASTE_YOUR_COMPLETE_SNS_TOPIC_ARN_HERE",
  "sns_region": "ap-south-1",

  "rekognition_collection_id": "attendance_collection",
  "rekognition_region": "ap-south-1"
}


Step 6:
curl -4 ifconfig.me
See ip and paste in rds inbound rules.
Test: python aws_test.py
If all 4 green, project is ready.

Step 7: Start project
python -m streamlit run Home.py
copy and paste host address. The app will open, just demonstrate then.


